notes               = "Untitled in source. The poem turns twice on خاطر (memory): rain falls so that you will bring the smell of adobe back to mind (به خاطر آوری), and the woman comes home having put the poet out of mind (از خاطر برده است). The English keeps 'mind' in both places so the hinge is audible. The addressee shifts mid-poem — plural یاران ('friends') and then a singular تو who rains — left unresolved, as the Persian leaves it. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

های... یاران...
تو می‌باری...
تا بوی کاهگل را
که فراموش کرده‌ای
به خاطر آوری.
باران ببار...
زنی را که دوست دارم
سفر می‌کند
و چون برگردد
مرا از خاطر برده است...
تهران، پاییز ۱۳۶۸

===machine===

Hey... friends...
You are raining...
so that you may bring to mind
the smell of straw-and-clay
that you have forgotten.
Rain, rain down...
The woman I love
goes travelling
and when she comes back
she has put me out of mind...
Tehran, autumn 1368

===lantern===

Hey... friends...
you are raining...
so that the smell of adobe
you have let go of
comes back to mind.
Rain, rain down...
The woman I love
is off travelling,
and when she comes back
she has put me out of mind...

Tehran, autumn 1368

